--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Description:
The nvsegvisual element renders the segmentation output produced by nvinfer or
nvinferserver. It maps the per-pixel class map carried in the segmentation
metadata to a color coded RGBA image of the configured width and height.
Refer to the DeepStream SDK documentation for a description of the plugin.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-requisites:
- GStreamer-1.0 Development package
- GStreamer-1.0 Base Plugins Development package

Install using:
   sudo apt-get install libgstreamer-plugins-base1.0-dev libgstreamer1.0-dev

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compiling and installing the plugin:

  $ Set CUDA_VER in the MakeFile as per platform.
  $ sudo make (sudo not required in case of docker containers)
  $ sudo make install (sudo not required in case of docker containers)

The plugin libnvdsgst_segvisual.so is installed at
/opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream/lib/gst-plugins/

Clear the GStreamer plugin cache after installing the plugin:
  $ rm -rf ~/.cache/gstreamer-1.0/

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
How to test:
Refer to the segmentation configuration files under
samples/configs/deepstream-app for reference pipelines that use nvsegvisual.
